Z||000005||AusFiero||07-22-2001||09:27 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by FieroLisa:<BR><B>Nokia sucks for one :-)<P>We don't even sell those phones anymore at Sprint PCS, otherwise I would help you out!</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>So what do you base that on Lisa? <BR>My brother inlaw owns a multi million dollar phone company and is a highly trained telecommunications technician im mobile services and land lines and they swear by 2 mobile phones makes only for quality and reliability. Ericsson and Nokia.<P>Please explain.<P><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero/ausfiero1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero" TARGET=_blank>My Fiero</A> | <A HREF="http://www.auto-alley.com" TARGET=_blank>Fiero Accessories</A>||202.139.20.3||reg||1
Z||000006||stimpy||07-22-2001||09:39 AM||||Uh-oh, the shite is goin down now. Seriously, no fighting in my thread please? I have sufficient self confidence that I'm not gonna let Lisa's comment force me into sobbing into my pillow because I bought a celphoe that she doesn't like. As DecadanceR pointed ou, my question does not point to a defect in the phone, merely an oversight on getting my service set up.<P>Now, unless anybody has cool sites from which to download free tones, I'd just as soon consider the topic closed.  ||||reg||1
Z||000007||p4n1c||07-22-2001||10:48 AM||||Actually Nokia and Ericsson are the top cell phone makers in the world.  Their UK phones are ten times better than the North American phones, but the Nokia phones are the best quality ones here.  <P>That's why Rogers/AT&T, Fido, etc only use Nokia and Ericsson and the reason you see more Nokia phones in peoples hands, in movies and rated top in reviews.<P>Now on topic for Stimpy's question.  I'd recommend getting a data cable and Nokia DataSuite, then you can take some MIDIs and convert them to ring tones and also upload a new graphic for your phone.  Double check though that your phone supports it, I think only the GSM phones can do the data cable upload of ring tones and graphics, TDMA/AMPS ones can't.  I think the 5165 does support it.  My 5190 did, but my 5160 doesn't(GSM versus TDMA/AMPS).<p>[This message has been edited by p4n1c (edited 07-22-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000008||AusFiero||07-22-2001||11:14 AM||||LOL no....no ****  stimpy. Just interested how someone can call Nokia sh1t when they are one of the best phones in the world.<P>I seem to recall a friend finding a really good site for downloading ringtones etc. I will ask here if she remembers where it is.||||reg||1
Z||000009||firstfiero||07-22-2001||11:19 AM||||    Not to argue with ya lisa...truthfully don't give a crap...but why do nokias get rated as the best cell phone consistantly over the years if they suck? What sucks about them?<P>------------------<BR><BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/firstfiero.gif"> ||||reg||5
Z||000010||DecadenceR||07-22-2001||11:51 AM||||Stimpy - Do a search on yahoo or Google for Mobile Ringtones, and you get lotsa hits, just make sure they send it to you by SMS. I had a really good site, but I can't find it anymore. So sad....<P>I LOVE my Nokia phone. First I had the 5100 that EVERYONE has, and I liked it but it was too big and no clip. So I got a Motorola StarTac, but that thing had NO battery life at all. I was charging it every other night. Then I recently got my Nokia 8260, and I LOVE this phone!!!!||||reg||1
